.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd September 25, 2026
.Dt SHUTDOWN 8
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm shutdown
.Nd close down the system at a given time
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl
.Op Fl h | p | r | k
.Op Fl o Op Fl n
.Ar time
.Op Ar warning-message ...
.Nm
.Fl C
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility takes the system down at
.Ar time ,
warning its users beforehand.
It waits in the background, recording its process ID in
.Pa /var/run/shutdown.pid .
Warnings go to the system console at 10, 5 and 2 hours, 1 hour, 45, 30,
20, 15, 10, 5, 3, 2 and 1 minutes, and 30 seconds before the time, together
with
.Ar warning-message .
Five minutes before, it creates
.Pa /etc/nologin ,
after which
.Xr login 1
refuses users other than the superuser.
.Pp
At
.Ar time
it asks
.Xr init 8
to stop the system: to reboot with
.Fl r ,
halt with
.Fl h ,
power off with
.Fl p ,
and with none of them, to take the system to single-user mode.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl
Read the warning message from the standard input, after any given on the
command line.
.It Fl C
Cancel the pending shutdown.
.It Fl h
Halt the system.
.It Fl k
Warn users and disable logins, but do not stop the system.
.Pa /etc/nologin
is left in place.
.It Fl n
With
.Fl o ,
do not synchronize the file systems.
.It Fl o
Run
.Xr reboot 8
.Fl q
instead of asking
.Xr init 8 ,
so no services are stopped.
Requires
.Fl h ,
.Fl p
or
.Fl r .
.It Fl p
Power the system off.
.It Fl r
Reboot the system.
.El
.Pp
.Ar time
is one of:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm now
Immediately.
.It Cm + Ns Ar minutes
That many minutes from now.
.It Ar hh Ns Cm \&: Ns Ar mm
Today at that time.
.It Oo Oo Oo Oo Oo Ar cc Oc Ns Ar yy Oc Ns Ar mm Oc Ns Ar dd Oc Ns Ar hh Oc Ns Ar mm
An absolute time; omitted fields keep their current values, and a
two-digit year below 69 is in the 21st century.
.El
.Pp
A time in the past is an error.
Only one shutdown may be pending; sending it
.Dv SIGINT
or
.Dv SIGTERM ,
as
.Fl C
does, cancels it and removes
.Pa /etc/nologin .
Only the superuser may use
.Nm .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /var/run/shutdown.pid -compact
.It Pa /etc/nologin
tells
.Xr login 1
not to admit users
.It Pa /var/run/shutdown.pid
the pending shutdown
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Reboot in 10 minutes, then change your mind:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# shutdown -r +10 "installing a new kernel"
# shutdown -C
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr login 1 ,
.Xr init 8 ,
.Xr rc 8 ,
.Xr reboot 8
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
utility appeared in
.Bx 4.0 .
This implementation was written for OxideBSD.
The
.Fl C
option is OxideBSD's;
.Fl c
remains reserved for power cycling, as in
.Fx ,
which OxideBSD does not support.
